Z||000000||samhitch||08-01-2001||01:11 PM||||Does anyone have any experience successfully repairing the plastic bumper material on Fieros? I have a tear on mine about three inches long. Will plastic welding techniques work or is it possible to solvent weld them? What is the plastic used for bumper and fenders?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Sam||||reg||5
Z||000001||88CoupeV6||08-01-2001||01:46 PM||||I found this stuff at autozone. It is a 2 part epoxy. It worked great on my bumper. I used it all over the car on any imperfections before it went to the paint shop. It had a 2 inch bumper tear. I also filled the holes for the Word pontiac I removed.<BR>Here is a pic.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fbr.jpg">  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">   <BR><B>Also 88 Yellow GT</B> :D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-01-2001||02:18 PM||||In my shop I use 3M #5895. its two tubes you mix equal parts. costs about $25. It says dry in 4 hours, but I always let it dry overnite. Ive fixed foot long rips, missing pieces, all with no prob.||||reg||1
